From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alfred Ben <e0958604@u.nus.edu>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:24:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] mcp: share one MCP server per project root

Every `codedb mcp` stdio session ran its own index process, so N agent
sessions on one repo held N copies of the index. `codedb mcp` now
forwards to one `mcp-server` per project root over a private Unix
socket; the server exits after CODEDB_MCP_IDLE_MS without clients.
CODEDB_MCP_SHARED=0 restores in-process serving, and any socket error
falls back to it.

- private socket dir, all inherited fds closed, key mismatch refused
- the word index is built once when concurrent sessions miss it
- a project that names the server's own root reuses the shared index
- ADR 0012 and docs/mcp.md, docs/cli.md describe the model

10 concurrent clients: 1 server at 179 MB warm (peak 227) plus 1.2 MB
per forwarder.
